            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Apart from built-in pickers in 'mini.pick' itself, there are [additional pickers in 'mini.extra'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e50cf9de614500a20e47cfc50e30a100042f91c3/doc/mini-extra.txt#L211). In particular, there is a [`treesitter`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e50cf9de614500a20e47cfc50e30a100042f91c3/doc/mini-extra.txt#L722) picker.\r\n\r\nSo after calling `require('mini.pick').setup()` and `require('mini.extra').setup()`, you can execute `:Pick treesitter` and then type `'function` to filter nodes that contain \"function\" in their name.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Apart from built-in pickers in 'mini.pick' itself, there are <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e50cf9de614500a20e47cfc50e30a100042f91c3/doc/mini-extra.txt#L211\">additional pickers in 'mini.extra'</a>. In particular, there is a <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e50cf9de614500a20e47cfc50e30a100042f91c3/doc/mini-extra.txt#L722\"><code class=\"notranslate\">treesitter</code></a> picker.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">So after calling <code class=\"notranslate\">require('mini.pick').setup()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">require('mini.extra').setup()</code>, you can execute <code class=\"notranslate\">:Pick treesitter</code> and then type <code class=\"notranslate\">'function</code> to filter nodes that contain \"function\" in their name.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Apart from built-in pickers in 'mini.pick' itself, there are additional pickers in 'mini.extra'. In particular, there is a treesitter picker.\nSo after calling require('mini.pick').setup() and require('mini.extra').setup(), you can execute :Pick treesitter and then type 'function to filter nodes that contain \"function\" in their name.",
